## Lore

The typical revolutionary fighting the Transgalactic Empire. The rebellion is
over a century old now, so a great many freedom fighters were born into a state
of war and are hardened veterans by their teens.

Most are fanatically dedicated to winning it, and have been taught since
childhood to hate the Transgalactic Empire and everything it stands for. That
hatred routinely extends to the entire kreeghor race, and to silhouettes.

## GM Notes

Available as a player character - the only class in this chapter the book offers
without asking for the Game Master''s approval first.

**At least two of the eight related skill picks must come from Espionage and two
from Rogue.** The app offers all eight freely; hold the player to it.

Elite units are issued **Naruni camouflage armor**, which this book names and
never stats. The equipment list offers the mega-damage suits the book does print;
swap it in if the character is elite.

The prejudice is worth playing. A freedom fighter raised in the Free World
Council has been taught to hate every kreeghor and every silhouette on sight -
and both of those are player races in this same chapter.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'freedom-fighter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'freedom-fighter';

